    secure:{title:'Security: FTP, FTPS, and SFTP are different',meta:['FTP plaintext','FTPS = FTP + TLS','SFTP = SSH protocol'],text:'Classic FTP exposes usernames, passwords, commands, and data. FTPS protects FTP with TLS. SFTP is not FTP; it is a separate file-transfer protocol inside SSH, commonly on port 22.',cmd:['AUTH TLS starts FTPS protection','Explicit FTPS often begins on port 21','SFTP normally uses SSH port 22'],data:['Use encrypted alternatives on real networks','Do not confuse FTPS with SFTP'],pulse:[465,42]}
